Chapter: ProbeOverapplyOneCaller

 The control for probe-overapply-two-callers.codex, and it exists to kill
 a confound rather than to show anything itself.

 COMPILER-18 records, under NOT ESTABLISHED, that "appending a third
 statement to an unrelated two-statement program stops its first statement
 from printing" -- so statement COUNT had to be excluded before a second
 call site could be blamed. This file has the same four statements as its
 pair; the third calls add3 instead of `sel`. Bare metal answers
 6, 12, 25, 15 -- correct throughout, 2026-08-25, seed 6CF4A8E0.


  add3 : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  add3 (a) (b) (c) = a + b + c

  sel : Integer -> (Integer, Integer -> Integer)
  sel (n) = add3 n

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
   print-line-uni ("control-flat: " & show (add3 1 2 3))
   print-line-uni ("first-call: " & show (sel 7 2 3))
   print-line-uni ("filler: " & show (add3 20 2 3))
   print-line-uni ("after: " & show (add3 4 5 6))
  end
